  "verbalization": "Ancistrobenomine A is shown to have a target relationship with Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which in turn is targeted by three different compounds: (4S,4aR,5S,8aR,9aS)-4a,5,6,7,8,8a,9,9a-Octahydro-4-hydroxy-9a-methoxy-3,4a,5-trimethylnaphtho(2,3-b)furan-2(4H)-one, Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate, and 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid. All three of these compounds are linked to Replicase polyprotein 1ab, suggesting a potential pathway through Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. The evidence indicates that Ancistrobenomine A may interact with this enzyme, which is a key component in the replication of viral RNA, and that this interaction could be a mechanism by which the compound exerts its effect on the replicase polyprotein 1ab. The relationship is supported by multiple independent pathways, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated."
